#heading(level: 1, numbering: none, outlined: true)[Acknowledgements]

I would like to thank Dr. Alexis Shakas and Dr. Johannes Aichele for their guidance and support throughout this project. Their expertise in ground-penetrating radar and time-lapse monitoring has been invaluable. I would like to thank Dr. Johannes Aichele in particular for providing me with the idea to look at phase changes, rather than amplitude changes, as a way to detect sub-wavelength displacements. Without this insight, the theory developed in this thesis would not have been possible. I would also like to thank Dr. Alexis Shakas for his guidance on the practical aspects of GPR data collection and in particular for providing me with the borehole GPR data used in this thesis. This extremely clean and well-documented dataset was crucial to proving the validity of the method developed in this thesis.
